==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|disconcert|ing}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌdɪskənˈsɜːtɪŋ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌdɪskənˈsɝtɪŋ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-disconcerting.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Tending to cause [[discomfort]], [[uneasiness]] or [[alarm]].
#: {{syn|en|unsettling|troubling|upsetting}}
#: {{ux|en|Even with a safety harness, losing one's grip that high up is '''disconcerting'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1920|author=w:Herman Cyril McNeile|title=Bulldog Drummond|chapter=1|passage="You must admit," he remarked, "that up to now our conversation has hardly proceeded along conventional lines. I am a complete stranger to you; another man who is a complete stranger to me speaks to you while we're at tea. You inform me that I shall probably have to kill him in the near future. The statement is, I think you will agree, a trifle '''disconcerting'''."}}

